Health care workers and organizers said ICE entered a Minneapolis hospital without a warrant and guarded/handcuffed a patient to a bed, raising concerns about interference with care and access to private areas. [LINK: ([60]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-60]

Federal agents tackled people and used chemical irritants and detained an educator [LINK: ([61]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-61]  outside  [LINK: (Roosevelt High School) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roosevelt_High_School_(Minnesota)]  in Minneapolis. Eyewitnesses said the agents were hitting people who were already on the ground.  [LINK: (Minneapolis Public Schools) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minneapolis_Public_Schools]  subsequently canceled classes for the remainder of the week. [LINK: ([62]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-62]

January 8
In a  [LINK: (McDonald's) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDonald%27s]  in Minneapolis's north side, a security guard blocked ICE from forcing their way behind the restaurant's counter without a warrant. [LINK: ([63]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-63] 
A video showed ICE agents raiding a  [LINK: (Target) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Target_Corporation]  store and arresting two workers in the Minneapolis suburb of  [LINK: (Richfield) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richfield,_Minnesota] . [LINK: ([64]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-64]  [LINK: ([65]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-65]  Both were US citizens, who were injured during the incident and released shortly after being detained. [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:21-31]

In a  [LINK: (McDonald's) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDonald%27s]  in Minneapolis's north side, a security guard blocked ICE from forcing their way behind the restaurant's counter without a warrant. [LINK: ([63]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-63]

A video showed ICE agents raiding a  [LINK: (Target) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Target_Corporation]  store and arresting two workers in the Minneapolis suburb of  [LINK: (Richfield) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richfield,_Minnesota] . [LINK: ([64]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-64]  [LINK: ([65]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-65]  Both were US citizens, who were injured during the incident and released shortly after being detained. [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:21-31]

January 9
An ICE agent threatened a pregnant  [LINK: (St. Louis Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Louis_Park,_Minnesota]  immigration attorney with a can of pepper spray and scanned her face after she requested that the agent leave the private parking lot of her law firm. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:0-6] 
Four members of the  [LINK: (Oglala Sioux) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oglala]  tribe were detained by ICE during a raid on a homeless encampment in Minneapolis. DHS refused to give tribal President Frank Star Comes Out more information about the detainees unless the tribe entered into an immigration enforcement agreement with ICE. One of the four detainees was released, and the other three were held at  [LINK: (Fort Snelling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Snelling] , the site where native prisoners were held during the  [LINK: (Dakota War of 1862) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakota_War_of_1862] . [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:24-35] 
A family reported that a father was detained by ICE while on his way to work, disrupting the family's livelihood and leaving them uncertain about his status and location. [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:22-33]

An ICE agent threatened a pregnant  [LINK: (St. Louis Park) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Louis_Park,_Minnesota]  immigration attorney with a can of pepper spray and scanned her face after she requested that the agent leave the private parking lot of her law firm. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:0-6]

Four members of the  [LINK: (Oglala Sioux) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oglala]  tribe were detained by ICE during a raid on a homeless encampment in Minneapolis. DHS refused to give tribal President Frank Star Comes Out more information about the detainees unless the tribe entered into an immigration enforcement agreement with ICE. One of the four detainees was released, and the other three were held at  [LINK: (Fort Snelling) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Snelling] , the site where native prisoners were held during the  [LINK: (Dakota War of 1862) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakota_War_of_1862] . [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:24-35]

A family reported that a father was detained by ICE while on his way to work, disrupting the family's livelihood and leaving them uncertain about his status and location. [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:22-33]

January 10
While tens of thousands of people protested against the activities of ICE in reaction to the killing of Renée Good, as part of a coordinated national protest movement targeting ICE and federal immigration enforcement practices, [LINK: ([66]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-66]  29 protesters were arrested. [LINK: ([67]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-67] 
A restaurant's surveillance video showed a worker described as legally authorized to work being seized by federal agents who appeared to have been waiting outside. [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:18-28]

While tens of thousands of people protested against the activities of ICE in reaction to the killing of Renée Good, as part of a coordinated national protest movement targeting ICE and federal immigration enforcement practices, [LINK: ([66]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-66]  29 protesters were arrested. [LINK: ([67]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-67]

A restaurant's surveillance video showed a worker described as legally authorized to work being seized by federal agents who appeared to have been waiting outside. [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:18-28]

January 11
An ICE agent threatened a man who said he was trying to get home, accusing the driver of following them and saying "Did you not learn from what just happened?" in reference to the killing of Renée Good. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:1-7] 
ICE arrested two US citizens engaged in a community patrol who were monitoring their activities. The agents sprayed pepper spray into the vent of the patrollers' car and smashed the car's windows. [LINK: ([68]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-68]  One patroller described his experience inside the Whipple Federal Building, where he said that food and bathroom breaks were rare, injured detainees were denied medical attention, and that DHS agents offered to "pay him money or extract favorable immigration outcomes on his behalf if he would give them the names and contact information of other illegal immigrants". The pair were released into an active protest outside the building after 8 hours of detention, and subsequently pepper sprayed alongside the other protesters. [LINK: ([41]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:29-41] 
In St Paul, ICE smashed the window of a Honduran national and dragged him from his car, also arresting a protestor out of the crowd that had formed to observe the arrest. [LINK: ([69]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-69]  On 14 January, his family said he was alive, but very injured and not receiving treatment, in a detention center in El Paso, Texas. [LINK: ([70]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:10-70] 
 [LINK: (Greg Bovino) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gregory_Bovino]  was booed and cursed at after using the bathroom at a Target in  [LINK: (Midway) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamline-Midway,_Saint_Paul] . [LINK: ([58]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:2-58]

An ICE agent threatened a man who said he was trying to get home, accusing the driver of following them and saying "Did you not learn from what just happened?" in reference to the killing of Renée Good. [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:1-7]

