ICE deployed to  [LINK: (Minneapolis-Saint Paul Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minneapolis%E2%80%93Saint_Paul_International_Airport] , establishing checkpoints to verify the documents of travelers and employees. [LINK: ([76]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-76]

January 14
Healthcare workers in the Twin Cities said that ICE agents were entering hospitals with detained individuals, worrying nurses and interfering with patient care by entering private areas of the hospital without a warrant. [LINK: ([77]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-77] 
A Woodbury, Minnesota real estate agent who spotted an ICE patrol and parked next to them at a shopping center had his car blocked in by ICE agents and was detained by them for three hours at the Whipple Federal Building. [LINK: ([78]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-78] 
A neighbor's home security camera captured an ICE arrest at a bus stop in South Minneapolis. The camera has also captured changes in the behavior of commuters, including people waiting around the corner until the bus comes or running home after getting off the bus, for fear of being picked up by ICE. [LINK: ([37]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:25-37] 
Aquila Elementary School was forced to change its pick-up procedures due to a persistent ICE presence at the school and at an apartment building across the street. One PTA member said that "Aquila teaches its kids to be kind, to be tolerant, to be thoughtful, to keep their hands to themselves, and none of those attributes are being modeled for them in the world outside their school," and that "Kids are missing school because ICE keeps cracking down on this city, this community, and specifically this neighborhood, these few blocks here, almost every day." [LINK: ([79]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-79] 
Agents forced their way into an apartment building, detaining a 17-year-old Columbia Heights student and her mother. [LINK: ([56]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-:4-56] 
 [LINK: (Death of Victor Manuel Diaz) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Victor_Manuel_Diaz]  at Camp East Montana. [LINK: ([57]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Metro_Surge#cite_note-VictorMD-AP-57]

